{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261112T174901Z_dev-01_flat_f687", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "In the SFDM benchmark (m_ψ = 47.75 GeV, m_h2 = 14.325 GeV, r = 0.3), the paper gives these h2 branching fractions: Br(h2→b b̄) = 0.7910, Br(h2→c c̄) = 0.1281 and Br(h2→τ⁺τ⁻) = 0.0797. The four-bottom final state accounts for about 62.6% of h2h2 decays. This matches (0.7910)² ≈ 0.626. The remaining combinations, including 2b2c and 2b2τ, make up the rest.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "7.2"}]}, "turns": 2, "seconds": 9.482, "tool_calls": 1, "tool_result_chars": 147086, "input_tokens": 67707, "output_tokens": 367, "parser_versions": ["3"], "ended_at": "2026-11-12T17:49:11+00:00"}
